Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||11-02-2001||11:47 PM||||i went to the salvage yard today looking for a set of tires and wheels because mine are badly weather checked because they sat on my fiero for 5 years. as i was looking at the sunbirds trying to find factory looking wheels i saw these on a 86 Z24 cavalier.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel2_1.jpg">  <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheels_3.jpg">  <P>those pictures i had to find on the net because i don't have a digital camera yet. but they are the exact same wheels as mine.<P><BR>i got them for $200 total and they have 4 brand new tires on them. two of them are 215 60 14 and the other two are 215 70 14. i am putting the 215 70's on the rear because i think it would look better that way.  <P>the clear coat is starting to chip off but it isn't too bad. when i repaint my 85 GT next year i will repaint the wheels too. and i will probably put the aluminum center caps from the fiero wheels on them since the fins and outside rim is aluminum.i already checked and found out they fit.  <P>(EDIT: its kinda hard to see but there are 4 fins on each spoke.)<P>you think i got a good deal on these wheels and tires?<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero_nightmare (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Flamberge||11-03-2001||04:26 AM||||The tires themselves are probably worth $200, nice job. I would have to see the rims on the Fiero to see if I liked it or not. Probably I wouldn't, to be honest, but you never know, and if you like it, that is all that matters. Way to go!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||14
